# Jarvis environment variables
#
# Copy this file to `.env` (which is gitignored) and fill in your own keys.
#
# GROQ_API_KEY is currently required for Jarvis to start (tools/groq_tool.py
# checks it at import). Once running, any Groq call that fails falls back to
# local Ollama automatically. BRAVE_API_KEY is only needed for web_search.
#
# ─── API keys ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# GROQ_API_KEY — Cloud LLM (Groq, free tier).
#   brain.py routes every request with gpt-oss-20b; agents use gpt-oss-120b
#   through tools/llm_tool.py.
#   Get one at: https://console.groq.com/keys
#
# BRAVE_API_KEY — Web search backend.
#   Used by tools/search_tool.py for Brave Search + AI summary.
#   Get one at: https://brave.com/search/api/
#
GROQ_API_KEY=
BRAVE_API_KEY=

# ─── Optional path overrides ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# JARVIS_BLENDER_PATH — full path to the Blender executable.
#   Default (Mac): /Applications/Blender.app/Contents/MacOS/Blender
#   Set this if Blender lives elsewhere (e.g. a Steam install).
#
# JARVIS_CLAUDE_CLI — full path to the Claude Code CLI binary.
#   Default: /usr/local/bin/claude
#   Used by the blender_claude agent. Only needed if `claude` is somewhere else.
#
# JARVIS_MEMORY_VAULT — full path to your Obsidian memory vault.
#   Default: a "Jarvis Memory" folder sitting next to the repo directory.
#   The vault holds personal data and lives outside the repo so it is never
#   committed. Set this if you keep your vault somewhere else.
#
# JARVIS_TRAINING_DATA — where the interaction logger writes training data.
#   Default: training_data/ inside the repo (gitignored). Point it elsewhere to
#   keep test runs out of your real dataset.
#
# JARVIS_BLENDER_PATH=
# JARVIS_CLAUDE_CLI=
# JARVIS_MEMORY_VAULT=
# JARVIS_TRAINING_DATA=
